<reference id="Installation-BACnet-4D4BCB61" xml:lang="en" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">Installation</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This chapter documents how to install the BACnet driver
to run in both a Supervisor (client) and remote station (server).</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">installation</indexterm></keywords></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section "><title class="- topic/title ">Prerequisites</title><ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li ">You  have a target host (remote
controller) that is licensed for the feature <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname>, or a PC host, which acts as a BACnet Supervisor. </li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">The Supervisor is licensed for <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">bacnet</apiname>.</p></li></ul><note type="note" class="- topic/note ">All platforms support the link layer types BACnet/IP,
BACnet/Ethernet, and BACnet/SC. BACnet MS/TP trunks are supported by various controllers, including those based on QNX and the <ph conkeyref="host_models/nc9000" class="- topic/ph "/>, among others. Separate licensing is required. </note></section><section class="- topic/section "><title class="- topic/title ">Modules</title><p class="- topic/p ">The palette provides four BACnet
modules.</p><table class="- topic/table "><tgroup cols="5" class="- topic/tgroup "><?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="891.00px"?><colspec colname="COLSPEC3" colwidth="0.84*" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="0.70*" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="col3" colwidth="0.88*" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="COLSPEC1" colwidth="0.93*" class="- topic/colspec "/><colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.45*" class="- topic/colspec "/><thead class="- topic/thead "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">Usage</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Palette name</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Network component name in the Nav tree</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">.jar file names in the modules folder</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Comments</entry></row></thead><tbody class="- topic/tbody "><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">BACnet functionality</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnet</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">BacnetNetwork</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnet-rt.jar, bacnetUtil-rt.jar, bacnet-ux.jar, bacnet-wb.jar</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">This module provides BACnet functionality to a server station
running on a remote controller.</entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">BACnet Advanced Workstation</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetAws</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">BacnetAwsNetwork</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetAws-rt.jar, bacnetAws-ux.jar, bacnetAws-wb.jar</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">This module provides BACnet functionality to a client station
running on a PC.</entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">BACnet Operator Workstation</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetOws</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">BacnetOwsNetwork</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetOws-rt.jar, bacnetOws-ux.jar, bacnetOws-wb.jar</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">This module provides BACnet functionality to a client station
running on a PC.</entry></row><row class="- topic/row "><entry class="- topic/entry ">BACnet Workstation</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetws</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">BacnetWsNetwork</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">bacnetMigrator-wb.jar</entry><entry class="- topic/entry ">Support for this legacy module ended with <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/NiagaraAX-3.7" class="- topic/keyword "/> and should not be used for new installations.</entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table></section></refbody></reference>